    "body": "<!-- relay-run-log -->\n**Relay run log** — issue #404\n\n- 2026-09-16 13:33Z — Relay picked up this issue for a BB worker run.\n- 2026-09-16 13:53Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #415 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed branch `bb/relay-404-get-healthz-gates-on-a-process-that-do-thr_6jg57a3fjx` to origin. ## Summary `GET /healthz` gated on the `agents` process's `process_heartbeats` row, but the `api` process (which serves `/healthz` from `serve.ts`) only ever UPSERTs a heartbeat row under its own name, `api`. In any deployment where the `agents` process isn't running alongside `api`, the health probe would report unhealthy even though the `api` process itself is perfectly healthy. ## Changes - `backend/services/semprec-api/src/healthzHandler.ts`: narrowed the freshness check from `\"agents\"` to `\"api\"`, matching the process this handler actually runs inside, and updated the doc comment accordingly. - `backend/services/semprec-api/src/__tests__/healthzHandler.test.ts`: updated existing tests to seed/assert against the `api` process, and added a test confirming `/healthz` stays healthy when the `agents` heartbeat is absent but `api`'s own heartbeat is fresh. - `backend/packages/data/src/health/processHeartbeats.ts`: updated a stale doc comment that referenced `agents` specifically. ## Testing - `backend`: `pnpm run verify` (lint, format check, build across all packages/services, unit tests, dependency-boundary check, integration tests — 97 files / 1181 tests, e2e tests — 5 tests) — all passed. - `web`: `pnpm run verify` (lint, format check, build, tests — 24 files / 187 tests) — all passed (no web files touched by this change). 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code) Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-16 14:01Z — Relay BB run is blocked and needs manual follow-up — it will not be retried automatically. Reason: could not request a re-run for code-review check \"code-review\": GitHub API /actions/runs/35105077805/rerun failed (403): {\"message\":\"Resource not accessible by integration\",\"documentation_url\":\"https://docs.github.com/rest/actions/workflow-runs#re-run-a-workflow\",\"status\":\"403\"} — manual follow-up needed: https://github.com/dvdtrsnk/semprec/runs/104824164586 Pushed branch `bb/relay-404-get-healthz-gates-on-a-process-that-do-thr_6jg57a3fjx` to origin. ## Summary `GET /healthz` gated on the `agents` process's `process_heartbeats` row, but the `api` process (which serves `/healthz` from `serve.ts`) only ever UPSERTs a heartbeat row under its own name, `api`. In any deployment where the `agents` process isn't running alongside `api`, the health probe would report unhealthy even though the `api` process itself is perfectly healthy. ## Changes - `backend/services/semprec-api/src/healthzHandler.ts`: narrowed the freshness check from `\"agents\"` to `\"api\"`, matching the process this handler actually runs inside, and updated the doc comment accordingly. - `backend/services/semprec-api/src/__tests__/healthzHandler.test.ts`: updated existing tests to seed/assert against the `api` process, and added a test confirming `/healthz` stays healthy when the `agents` heartbeat is absent but `api`'s own heartbeat is fresh. - `backend/packages/data/src/health/processHeartbeats.ts`: updated a stale doc comment that referenced `agents` specifically. ## Testing - `backend`: `pnpm run verify` (lint, format check, build across all packages/services, unit tests, dependency-boundary check, integration tests — 97 files / 1181 tests, e2e tests — 5 tests) — all passed. - `web`: `pnpm run verify` (lint, format check, build, tests — 24 files / 187 tests) — all passed (no web files touched by this change). 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code) Relay-Step-Status: pass Remove the `agent:blocked` label from this issue once it's addressed to let Relay pick it up again.",
